/E (Initially a reluctant piano student who preferred to play baseball, Ellington caught the bug after hearing ragtime pianists playing along U Street in places like Frank Holidays Pool Hall, next door to the Howard Theater. He formed his first small band as a teenager, playing in and around DC and out into the neighboring small towns of Virginia and Maryland, before striking out for the New York City. )
