/E (Soon she was running her own touring big-band, Blanche Calloway & Her Joy Boys, reputed to be the first woman ever to lead an all-male jazz big band. The Joy Boys ranked in the Top 10 US bands of 1933. Her success came to an end when she was arrested and jailed in Mississippi for using a whites-only bathroom. When she got out the band had absconded with the vehicles, money and instruments, so Blanche returned to New York and formed an all-women big band. )
