/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (One cold morning Getz arrived at National Airport and made his way to the church were Charlie and his band were gathered. An unusual line up of two drummers, two bass players Charlies regular bassist Keeter Betts and his younger brother, Joe Byrd. The now familiar sound was deemed so unusual that it needed extra hands! Within three hours the album was recorded, with three microphones, to a reel-to-reel tape recorder in the corridor. The engineer edited the tapes, handed over the master and everyone left, with no high expectations of what might happen next. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
